# Tests for the Elderly_and_disabled module

Run with `clerk test`. Named scopes with concrete numbers (issue #30), worked out
by hand line by line from Schedule R (`sources/forms-instructions/f1040sr--2024.pdf`
p 2) and its instructions (`i1040sr--2024.pdf` pp R-5 to R-7). The oracle comparison
is `make difftest SCOPE=elderly_and_disabled`.

> Using Types
> Using Elderly_and_disabled as E

## Helper: one Schedule R run

`pd` and `sd` say that the primary or secondary filer is retired on permanent and
total disability with taxable disability income `pinc` or `sinc` (and has W-2
wages, and no mandatory retirement age). `p65` and `s65` are the ages. `tax` is
Credit Limit Worksheet line 3.

```catala
declaration scope Run:
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  input apart condition
  input p65 condition
  input s65 condition
  input pd condition
  input pinc content money
  input sd condition
  input sinc content money
  input agi content money
  input ss content money
  input o13b content money
  input tax content money
  sr scope E.ScheduleR
  output edc_line1 condition
  output edc_line2 condition
  output edc_line3 condition
  output edc_line4 condition
  output edc_line5 condition
  output edc_line6 condition
  output edc_line7 condition
  output edc_line8 condition
  output edc_line9 condition
  output edc_filing_status_amt content money
  output status_based_disability_income content money
  output lesser content money
  output edc_total_non_taxable_amount content money
  output edc_exemption_amount content money
  output edc_magi content money
  output edc_half_magi content money
  output edc_adjusted_credit_amount content money
  output edc_net_credit_amount content money
  output net_edc_amount content money
  output edc_tax_liability_limit content money
  output total_edc content money
  output agi_limit content money
  output nontaxable_limit content money
  output qualified condition
  output receiving condition

scope Run:
  definition sr.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition sr.lived_apart_all_year equals apart
  definition sr.primary_age65_or_older equals p65
  definition sr.secondary_age65_or_older equals s65
  definition sr.primary_answers equals E.DisabilityAnswers {
    -- is_retired_on_perm_or_total_disability: pd
    -- employer_has_mandatory_retirement_age: false
    -- has_met_employer_mandatory_retirement_age: false
    -- are_payments_taxable_disability_income: pd
    -- writable_total_taxable_disability_amount: pinc
    -- has_w2_wages: pd
  }
  definition sr.secondary_answers equals E.DisabilityAnswers {
    -- is_retired_on_perm_or_total_disability: sd
    -- employer_has_mandatory_retirement_age: false
    -- has_met_employer_mandatory_retirement_age: false
    -- are_payments_taxable_disability_income: sd
    -- writable_total_taxable_disability_amount: sinc
    -- has_w2_wages: sd
  }
  definition sr.agi equals agi
  definition sr.non_taxable_social_security_benefits equals ss
  definition sr.self_reported_non_taxable_payments equals o13b
  definition sr.credit_limit_worksheet_line_3 equals tax
  definition edc_line1 equals sr.edc_line1
  definition edc_line2 equals sr.edc_line2
  definition edc_line3 equals sr.edc_line3
  definition edc_line4 equals sr.edc_line4
  definition edc_line5 equals sr.edc_line5
  definition edc_line6 equals sr.edc_line6
  definition edc_line7 equals sr.edc_line7
  definition edc_line8 equals sr.edc_line8
  definition edc_line9 equals sr.edc_line9
  definition edc_filing_status_amt equals sr.edc_filing_status_amt
  definition status_based_disability_income equals sr.status_based_disability_income
  definition lesser equals sr.lesser_of_filing_status_amount_and_taxable_disability_income
  definition edc_total_non_taxable_amount equals sr.edc_total_non_taxable_amount
  definition edc_exemption_amount equals sr.edc_exemption_amount
  definition edc_magi equals sr.edc_magi
  definition edc_half_magi equals sr.edc_half_magi
  definition edc_adjusted_credit_amount equals sr.edc_adjusted_credit_amount
  definition edc_net_credit_amount equals sr.edc_net_credit_amount
  definition net_edc_amount equals sr.net_edc_amount
  definition edc_tax_liability_limit equals sr.edc_tax_liability_limit
  definition total_edc equals sr.total_edc
  definition agi_limit equals sr.edc_agi_limit
  definition nontaxable_limit equals sr.edc_non_taxable_limit
  definition qualified equals sr.qualified_for_credit_for_elderly_and_disabled
  definition receiving equals sr.is_receiving_edc
```

## Cases

Issue #30: single age 66, AGI $10,000, no nontaxable social security: line 16 =
10,000 - 7,500 = 2,500, line 17 = 1,250, line 19 = 5,000 - 1,250 = 3,750, line 20
= 15% x 3,750 = 562.50, rounded to $563. Single, AGI $17,500: not qualified (the
AGI test is strict). Married filing jointly with both spouses 65 or older: AGI
limit $25,000 (24,000 gives 7,500 - 7,000 = 500, so $75; 25,000 gives none).
Married filing separately, lines 8 and 9: $3,750 initial amount, $5,000 exemption,
only if the spouses lived apart all year. The instructions' examples: Jesse (p R-5,
credit $51) and Riley and Parker (p R-6, no credit).

Other lines: MFJ box 7 (one spouse 65 or older, the other not disabled) has the
$20,000 AGI limit; box 6 line 11 adds $5,000 to the disabled spouse's income
(instructions Example 1 of Part III, $9,000); boxes 4 and 5 cap line 12 at the
disability income; nontaxable social security and self-reported nontaxable
payments reduce line 19 and, at $5,000 for a single filer, remove the credit.

```catala
